 "methodology": [
  "Spawn the robot, a 0.05 m-radius static sphere at 600 K (reproduce/hot_sphere.sdf) and the warehouse fire model at 600 K (fire model with @INITIAL_TEMPERATURE_K@ = 600.0), both parked below the floor.",
  "Bridge /clock, /tf, /odom, /thermal/image_raw and /thermal/camera_info; run a static base_link -> thermal_link transform with the launch-file arguments; run the installed operational fire_detection with use_sim_time.",
  "For each case (reproduce/cases.json): read the robot model and thermal_link poses from /world/warehouse_a/pose/info, place the target with /world/warehouse_a/set_pose at the commanded camera-frame azimuth (az, + = left), elevation (el, + = up) and range (dist) from the lens (fire cone: base on the floor, horizontal range), then take the 5 /thermal/observations frames stamped at least 0.4 s of sim time after the move. u and v are the medians of the largest region centroid.",
  "Read the true poses again after the measurement (robot_world, thermal_link_in_model, target_world: position [x, y, z], orientation [x, y, z, w]). Evaluation is offline: transform target_world into the thermal_link frame using these Gazebo poses (not /odom, which is not world-aligned).",
  "Robot configurations: (-1, 0, yaw pi) facing the open west area, then (-1.5, -1, yaw 2.6). Robot stationary, no cmd_vel."
 ],
